card = cocoon-open.mcd
# cocoon-open boots from a seeded card (tools/seed_card.py from secret-c04.mcd: scene 0, region index 43 (HK_REGION_ID counts from 1: 44), x 57.15,
# y 58.39, facing right) under King's Pass's Lifeblood cocoon, jumps and strikes up once: the cocoon opens
# and answers with its spatters, globs and cap (the break-effect pool), the Kill shake and its two bugs.
# Seeded, so it proves the cocoon's reaction, not the way to it. The tape is 380 polls long
# (mktape: 9:start:1,12:cross:1,260:cross:30,278:up+square:3).
HK_LIFEBLOOD_OPENED = 1
HK_REGION_ID = 44
HK_SAVE_LOADED = 1
HK_DEATHS = 0
# The cocoon's burst (42 bubbles, 9 globs, the splat, the strike) spawns 59 particles.
HK_PARTICLES_SPAWNED >= 59
pacing = 104
frame_time = 301
long_frames = 2
# 2026-10-29 doorways: 94 to 102 over 2 vblanks on the same tree with the lazy runner family (293 of 120 frames against 282 of 125); variants of the draw's pad poll gave 97 to 102, a one-frame phase flip of the burst, so the ceiling is 104.
